1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Episode 1

3
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:37,500
Somewhere in America

4
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:03,420
Invincible Eagle

5
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:05,820
Crimson Holy Light

6
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,340
I will Surpass you!

7
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,740
In the eyes of the World,

8
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:37,020
my Western Speed Style is the most powerful.

9
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:39,900
I'll be back for the next Tournament.

10
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:46,140
Jianghai City, China

11
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:14,460
Mickey, I know exactly what you're up to.

12
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:16,380
You just want to get taller, fast.

13
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,300
So you can look like the older kids.

14
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:20,700
And really show off your Yo-Yo skills.

15
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:24,540
But your body is going to grow at its own pace.

16
00:03:24,800 --> 00:03:26,940
It's a natural process, right?

17
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:29,340
You can't just hang from the monkey bars
and expect to force yourself taller.

18
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,740
That's not how it works.

19
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:34,140
But this came from Matthew!

20
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:37,470
He said if I hang from it for 3 months,

21
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:38,810
I could grow 20 centimeters.

22
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:43,230
That's nonsense. Matthew, Matthew!

23
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,670
Is everything Matthew says right?

24
00:03:44,680 --> 00:03:46,140
So by his logic, we should
all just hang from the bars?

25
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:47,580
All of us, dangling up there.

26
00:03:48,220 --> 00:03:49,500
We'd look like salted fish drying on a rack.

27
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:51,420
And it's not a good look, either.

28
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:56,220
You know the idiom,
"Pulling up the seedlings to help them grow"?

29
00:03:57,160 --> 00:04:00,060
But Coach Tony, that's about pulling up.

30
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:03,420
I'm hanging down. It's completely different.

31
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:07,260
Different? I don't see a difference.
It's exactly the same.

32
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:12,060
Every day after class, you're hogging the monkey bars.

33
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:14,430
You're blocking the other kids from practicing.

34
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:15,900
You just hang there, completely still,

35
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:19,380
like a zombie.

36
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:37,800
I'm just getting old, you know.

37
00:04:41,320 --> 00:04:43,740
So, what do you think?
That Sparrowhawk Flip was pretty smooth, right?

38
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,660
What do you have to say about that?

39
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:49,020
Old Li, you're still messing
around with that Diabolo?

40
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:50,940
Didn't you say your precious Grandson,

41
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:52,380
Leo, is coming home today?

42
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:55,260
Yeah, I've known Leo since the day he was born.

43
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:58,620
When he was 5, he went off to
America with his Mom and Dad.

44
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,540
After all these years, he's still just a kid.

45
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,420
You should hurry up and go meet him.

46
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:08,220
There's no need. He's a man of
the World now, you know.

47
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:11,350
He's probably been on more
planes than we have been on trains.

48
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,940
Anyway, his Dad gave him the address.

49
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:18,300
They said he can get home by himself.
No need to pick him up.

50
00:05:19,040 --> 00:05:20,220
The City's changed so much.

51
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:23,580
If I don't go out for a few days,
I barely recognize the streets.

52
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:25,020
It might be hard for him to find.

53
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:28,380
Don't worry about it. When he was 10,

54
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:31,260
he and his Dad went travelling
across the Country with just a map.

55
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,630
Jianghai is a tiny little place.

56
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:35,100
He won't get lost.

57
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:37,500
Alright, let's get back to practice.

58
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,940
Several of the girls have filed complaints about you.

59
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,340
I bet it was Mini who snitched on me.

60
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:08,700
Your sister's just looking out for you.

61
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:12,060
What does me hanging there have to do with them?

62
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:13,980
Don't try to twist this around, okay?

63
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:16,380
The bars are for everyone to use.

64
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:18,750
Hogging the bars and blocking
others from practicing is not okay.

65
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:19,740
That's just unacceptable.

66
00:06:21,160 --> 00:06:23,100
And today, I'm not just asking you.

67
00:06:23,740 --> 00:06:24,540
This is an Official warning.

68
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:26,520
If you don't change your ways,

69
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:30,750
your punishment will be to perform

70
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,220
300 repetitions of the Yo-Yo Basics.

71
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:36,060
Coach Tony? Have you seen Matthew?

72
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,940
Matthew again? Why would he be here with me?

73
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,340
He said you told him to come
to your office after Class.

74
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:44,220
Since when did I say that?

75
00:06:45,160 --> 00:06:45,660
He's really not here.

76
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,020
I told you, he's not here.

77
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:53,340
Okay, okay, okay.

78
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,260
These are important files. Stop snooping.

79
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,180
Can't you see I'm busy here?

80
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:00,060
Go on, get out of here. Go.

81
00:07:10,880 --> 00:07:11,580
This is ridiculous.

82
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,420
They treat the PE Room
like it's a game of hide-and-seek.

83
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,820
No one even knocks anymore.

84
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:19,740
The PE Department gets zero Respect.

85
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:21,660
Absolutely none.

86
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:27,900
Mickey.

87
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:29,820
Have you given it any more thought?

88
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:32,220
I have, Coach Tony.

89
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:35,100
What you're saying is, I should
just let nature take its course, right?

90
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,940
Looks like you understand me perfectly.

91
00:07:39,400 --> 00:07:41,820
I get the logic, Coach Tony, I really do. But,

92
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:43,740
look at my height.

93
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:47,550
There are some Yo-Yo tricks I just
can't pull off because I'm so short.

94
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:49,980
That's why my flow is always a little bit off.

95
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:54,780
It seems like my height is
the only thing holding me back

96
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,590
from becoming a Top-Tier Player.

97
00:07:57,400 --> 00:07:58,500
Don't say that.

98
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:00,990
To master the Yo-Yo,

99
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,430
height isn't a factor at all.

100
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:03,420
Because for any height,

101
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:04,800
there's a string length that fits you.

102
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:08,700
The real key is developing your feel for the Yo-Yo.

103
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,100
That actually makes a lot of sense.

104
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:13,500
Hey, Coach, let me ask you something...

105
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:15,690
What's with the secrecy? Spit it out.

106
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,780
Could you maybe teach me a few tricks... in private?

107
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:23,550
Teach you privately?

108
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:24,510
Yeah, exactly!

109
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:26,460
I'm talking about your Secret Yo-Yo Techniques.

110
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:28,860
Not a chance.

111
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:32,190
If you want to be a great Yo-Yo player,

112
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,620
you've got to put in the work and train hard. Right?

113
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:36,540
It's only through your own hard work and practice,

114
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,460
once you've mastered the
fundamentals and your own Style-

115
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:42,780
Whatever, if you're not going to teach me,
no need to get all worked up about it.

116
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:44,700
I just... I...

117
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:47,100
Hey Tony, are you busy?

118
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:48,540
Principal Qian.

119
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,900
Just giving a student some advice.

120
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,270
Principal Qian! You haven't set foot in the here

121
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,260
for at least 2 or 3 months!

122
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,180
The work around this School keeps me busy.

123
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,620
Oh, of course, of course.

124
00:08:59,080 --> 00:09:00,060
So, what brings you here today?

125
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:02,940
I have something important to discuss with you, naturally.

126
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:06,780
Take a look. It's an urgent memo about the City-Wide

127
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:09,660
Autumn Yo-Yo Tournament that's coming up.

128
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,100
The Yo-Yo Tournament!

129
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:12,310
Let me see! Let me see!

130
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,910
This is an Official School document.
How can you read it?

131
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:16,390
Alright, We're done here. Head out.

132
00:09:17,320 --> 00:09:18,270
Goodbye, Principal!

133
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:19,260
Yeah, see ya.

134
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:21,180
That kid...

135
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:22,620
Please, have a seat.

136
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,380
Approved by the City Education Bureau.

137
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:30,270
The All-City Yo-Yo Tournament is scheduled to be

138
00:09:30,280 --> 00:09:33,150
held in the second half of this year.

139
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:35,070
And adding on to the Individual Event from last year,

140
00:09:35,480 --> 00:09:36,630
a Team Event has been added.

141
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,910
All participating Schools are to prepare

142
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:40,380
and strive for the best results.

143
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:44,220
Chengnan High School, Xinjian Middle School,
Jianghai High School...

144
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:48,540
Chengnan High is on the list too?

145
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,380
Yeah. They're our old rivals.

146
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:57,440
And isn't that Sarah an alum of your Sports Academy?

147
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:01,980
I heard she's really something else.

148
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:05,820
Principal, I'm not worried about her.
What I'm thinking is,

149
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:08,220
shouldn't our School immediately

150
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:10,140
form an official School Yo-Yo Team?

151
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,020
Don't worry. I completely agree with you.

152
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:15,420
The School Administration has already signed off on this.

153
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,000
Really?

154
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:20,220
That's fantastic! Thank you Principal.

155
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:21,660
No need to thank me.

156
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,060
As the Principal,

157
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:26,460
it's my duty to care about the
Students' extracurricular activities.

158
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:29,820
That's why the School has decided

159
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:32,220
to put me in charge of leading this initiative.

160
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:35,580
And I personally requested that
you be appointed as the Coach.

161
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:37,800
Me? The Coach?

162
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:43,740
Monica!

163
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:47,100
You need to focus on controlling the Yo-Yo.

164
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:49,500
My mom says that

165
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:51,870
I need to cultivate a sense of artistry.

166
00:10:51,880 --> 00:10:54,300
You should always strive for perfect form and spirit.

167
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:59,100
Last year, we took home the Individual Champion title.

168
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:01,500
Chengnan High School came second place.

169
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:07,260
This time, we need to do everything
we can to win the Team Event.

170
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:09,660
I won't let everyone down.

171
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:12,540
I'm going to form the Jianghai Team right away,

172
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:13,980
and use the summer break

173
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:15,420
to put them through an intense Training Camp.

174
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:18,300
We've got to bring glory to Jianghai High!

175
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,400
Great!

176
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:21,660
I've always known you were the right person for the job.

177
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:25,020
Especially that book you wrote a few years back...

178
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:28,860
What was it called... that
"Something-Something Training Manual"?

179
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:30,300
That's some impressive stuff.

180
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Wow!

181
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:35,580
I gave you that copy of it last year.

182
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:37,020
The Secret Yo-Yo Training Manual.

183
00:11:37,660 --> 00:11:38,460
You never responded.

184
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:41,310
I just assumed you didn't think it was a priority.

185
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:43,260
Looks like I completely misunderstood you.

186
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:45,180
Come on! Of course I read it.

187
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:00,540
Alright, alright, Coach.

188
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:02,940
It's settled then. I'm heading out.

189
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:06,040
Uh Principal,

190
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:07,260
I just had one more question.

191
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:09,660
What about funding for the School Team,

192
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:11,580
a place to train... all of those things.

193
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,460
Oh. Well, about that... here's the thing.

194
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:15,600
Normally,

195
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,780
the School would be able to cover all of that for you.

196
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:21,180
But, you see, the timing is just awful.

197
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:23,100
The School is planning to renovate

198
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:25,020
all the Buildings on Campus over summer break.

199
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:27,920
It's a huge project for the Students' development.

200
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:32,220
So, most of the budget and the Training Space...

201
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:35,100
that's something you will have
to figure out on your own.

202
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Principal...

203
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:38,940
How am I supposed to do that?

204
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:41,340
Principal, what about the Team Uniforms?

205
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:43,260
And our Competition Gear. We still need that.

206
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:45,180
Yes, yes, of course you need those.

207
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:47,100
Not just any Uniforms and Gear, either.

208
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:49,020
They need to be Stylish. Trendy.

209
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:52,380
Right, but... the funding...

210
00:12:55,240 --> 00:12:56,220
Ah, come on now, Coach.

211
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:57,660
This is the status of the market economy.

212
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:59,580
You can go out there and

213
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:00,920
look for some Sponsors.

214
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:02,000
Me?

215
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:03,980
Yeah, I know how capable you are.

216
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:05,820
Otherwise,

217
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,670
why would I have entrusted you with such

218
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:10,140
a difficult and important responsibility?

219
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:13,980
I have complete faith you can pull this off.

220
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,900
Okay, I'm off now.

221
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:19,260
Principal! Principal! Wait, this...

222
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:25,980
I guess I'll have to find a way to make it work.

223
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,000
Coach!

224
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:37,500
Why are you still here?

225
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,000
Coach,

226
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:40,860
You have to put me on the Team.

227
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:42,780
And my Sister, too.

228
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,700
That all depends on how you behave.

229
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:46,620
Don't worry, Coach.

230
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,540
I won't hog the monkey bars anymore.

231
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:50,430
Okay, okay.

232
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:51,900
That's enough out of you. Head on home.

233
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Got it!

234
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,700
Hey listen!

235
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:01,980
Until I Officially announce the formation of the Team,

236
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:03,900
you have to keep this quiet.

237
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:04,860
Understood?

238
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,780
I don't really get it.

239
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:10,110
I just mean you can't let anyone

240
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:11,580
with a big mouth find out.

241
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:13,980
Oh, I get it now.

242
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:16,380
You especially can't let
that blabbermouth Popcorn know.

243
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:19,740
Just keep it to yourself and that's it.

244
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,140
I'm still confused.

245
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:23,580
Starting a School Team isn't a bad thing.

246
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:25,500
Why can't she know about it?

247
00:14:26,440 --> 00:14:27,420
How can you be so dense?

248
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:28,860
If Monica finds out,

249
00:14:29,320 --> 00:14:31,740
then every single Yo-Yo fan in the entire School

250
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:34,140
will be crammed into my Office by tomorrow morning.

251
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,060
Oh, I get it now.

252
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:37,500
Don't worry, Coach.

253
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:38,910
I guarantee this stays

254
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,380
between me and my Sister.

255
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,750
Alright, get out of here.

256
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:43,740
See ya, Coach.

257
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:45,000
See ya.

258
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:53,820
"Find Sponsors."

259
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:56,700
Easier said than done.

260
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:17,340
Sarah, oh Sarah

261
00:15:18,360 --> 00:15:19,740
I beat you last year.

262
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,180
And you're still bitter about it.

263
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:23,580
This year, I'll show you

264
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:25,500
exactly how I win the Team Event.

265
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:32,220
Let's see you call me an amateur then.

266
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:40,600
Sis.

267
00:16:10,120 --> 00:16:12,060
No money. No place to train.

268
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,460
What am I supposed to do now?

269
00:16:18,280 --> 00:16:20,700
Looks like I'll have to call in
a favour from an old classmate.

270
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,270
What's your problem?

271
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:31,260
Sis, come here, come on.

272
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:40,380
Good, Popcorn didn't follow us.

273
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,780
Sis, I've got huge news.

274
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:44,220
What kind of news?

275
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:45,630
I still need to practice.

276
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:47,580
Calm down. Just listen.

277
00:16:47,890 --> 00:16:48,540
I'm telling you,

278
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,460
this is way more important
than your Practice Session.

279
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
But...

280
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:54,780
No one else can know.

281
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:56,700
Well, spit it out already!

282
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Sis,

283
00:16:58,020 --> 00:17:00,540
The School's about to start an Official Yo-Yo Team.

284
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:01,980
It'll be called the Jianghai Team.

285
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:04,280
And Coach Tony is going to be the Head Coach.

286
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:05,300
Ah!

287
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:09,660
Hey! Just because you're excited doesn't
mean you have to shout it from the rooftops.

288
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:12,060
Be careful, or that loudmouth Popcorn might hear you.

289
00:17:12,520 --> 00:17:13,500
You know how she is.

290
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:15,420
She'll blab it to the whole World.

291
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:18,300
Sis, did you know? The School's starting a Team.

292
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:20,190
It's definitely to prepare

293
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:21,660
for this year's Autumn Yo-Yo Tournament.

294
00:17:22,120 --> 00:17:24,060
And this year, they've added a Team Event.

295
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:27,420
I bet anyone in the whole School can try out for it.

296
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,340
We've got to step up our practice, too.

297
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:32,220
I've been thinking, sis.

298
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:33,660
Out of all the girls in School,

299
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:36,540
you and Popcorn are the only ones with any real skill.

300
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,940
Actually, Popcorn might even
be a little better than you.

301
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:43,260
But... I don't think Popcorn
will actually make the Team.

302
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,620
Because even Coach Tony is scared of her big mouth.

303
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:49,500
Mickey, don't talk about people like that.

304
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:50,940
I'm not making it up.

305
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,860
She's like a total chatterbox parrot.

306
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:57,400
But... her skills are actually pretty solid right?

307
00:17:58,600 --> 00:18:01,020
Sis, stop always taking her side.

308
00:18:01,380 --> 00:18:01,980
Her Yo-Yo skills are

309
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:03,900
barely above average, at best.

310
00:18:04,360 --> 00:18:05,820
I could beat her with my "Ferris Wheel" combo

311
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:07,260
in less than 3 moves.

312
00:18:12,400 --> 00:18:13,200
But!

313
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:16,380
Then again, if you really think about it,

314
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:21,180
deep down, Monica really does have a good heart.

315
00:18:22,120 --> 00:18:24,060
She's passionate and brave.

316
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:28,860
She's open-minded, always willing to help,
and she gets great grades.

317
00:18:29,320 --> 00:18:30,300
She never holds it against her classmates

318
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:32,220
when they give her honest criticism.

319
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:34,140
And the best part is,

320
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:37,020
she's always treating everyone to popcorn.

321
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:39,420
How could a classmate like that

322
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:42,780
not make the Team? How could she not make it?

323
00:18:48,700 --> 00:18:49,500
What are you doing?

324
00:18:49,960 --> 00:18:51,900
So what if I've got a big mouth?

325
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:05,340
Looks like by tomorrow, the whole School is gonna know.

326
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:10,140
Not tomorrow. By tonight.

327
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:19,260
That's him! Stop! Stop right there!

328
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:23,100
Need a tire fixed?

329
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,940
I don't even have a bike. What would I need fixed?

330
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:30,300
That's the guy! Stop that thief!

331
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:32,700
He stole my wallet! Grab him!

332
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:34,140
Stop! Stop!

333
00:19:34,600 --> 00:19:35,580
Stop! Thief!

334
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:41,340
That's him! The thief! Get him!

335
00:19:42,180 --> 00:19:43,740
Run! Run! Where do you think you're going?

336
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:57,660
Stop that thief! He can't get away!

337
00:19:58,600 --> 00:20:00,060
Quick, quick, quick! Grab him! Grab him!

338
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:03,000
Stop!

339
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:11,580
Stop him! Stop that thief!

340
00:20:12,040 --> 00:20:13,500
That's him! He stole my wallet!

341
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:15,390
Stop, thief! Stop! Stop!

342
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:16,860
Stop him! Stop the thief!

343
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:19,000
Stop!

344
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:24,540
Stop, thief!

345
00:20:25,660 --> 00:20:26,940
Grab him! Get him!

346
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:30,780
Stay back! Don't come any closer!

347
00:20:30,840 --> 00:20:32,220
I... I didn't steal anything.

348
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:33,630
It was you!

349
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:34,590
I was just buying something,

350
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,060
and he was crowding me, bumping into me.

351
00:20:36,700 --> 00:20:37,980
That doesn't prove I took your wallet!

352
00:20:38,720 --> 00:20:39,420
Then why'd you run?

353
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:41,340
I... I'm in a hurry.

354
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:42,780
My... my mom is sick.

355
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:44,220
My mom's sick and in the Hospital.

356
00:20:44,680 --> 00:20:45,660
I have to go see my mom in the hospital.

357
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:47,580
Please, you've got to let me go! Let me go!

358
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:49,000
Liar!

359
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:49,980
Give me back my wallet!

360
00:20:50,440 --> 00:20:51,420
Let's take him to the Police!

361
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:54,780
Yeah, take him to the Police Station!

362
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:56,220
You... you're backing me into a corner.

363
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:57,660
I... I know kung fu.

364
00:20:58,880 --> 00:20:59,580
I know kung fu!

365
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:01,500
Don't pretend you're some kind of Martial Arts Master.

366
00:21:02,240 --> 00:21:02,940
Give me back my wallet.

367
00:21:05,320 --> 00:21:06,780
If you keep pushing me...

368
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:08,670
If you keep this up, I won't be so nice!

369
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:09,660
Drop it! Drop it! Put it down!

370
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:12,540
Stay back! Don't come any closer!

